  "entry": "10665-67344",
  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-000",
      "source": "sections/sec-000-a-public-health-solution-that-works.md",
      "source_hash": "d9ca380b65e45c104481ff8405cb6b1d3cfb47284fa6f6ac30219f80cf827da0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that mother-to-child HIV transmission has fallen below 2% in industrialised countries through antiretroviral drugs, elective Caesarean section and replacement feeding. It cites Thailand's fall in paediatric AIDS cases since prevention programmes began in 1997, alongside falling HIV prevalence among pregnant women.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-001",
      "source": "sections/sec-001-the-ungass-declaration-of-commitment.md",
      "source_hash": "179a39738a9e57e1f1fa445094c96cb967f2344d00976f2f35003e8e754d2796",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Quotes the 2001 UNGASS commitment to cut the share of infants infected with HIV by 20% by 2005 and 50% by 2010, with a chart of Thailand's declining paediatric AIDS cases. It begins listing needed interventions, starting with primary prevention of HIV among women, including during pregnancy and breastfeeding.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-002",
      "source": "sections/sec-002-prevention-of-unintended-pregnancies-among-hiv-i.md",
      "source_hash": "c7cb97f280fd26ac4b5781a1bfb1778f6b811132f5b9a6d8ee892c1817417dae",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Continues the list of interventions, calling for stronger family planning to prevent unintended pregnancies among women with HIV, most of whom do not know their status. It describes the package to prevent transmission to infants, including antiretrovirals, safer delivery, infant-feeding counselling and HIV testing, and stresses care and support for mothers and families.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "source": "sections/sec-003-a-framework-for-action-to-prevent-hiv-infection.md",
      "source_hash": "554dd7aed88fb1b56fa3a05f3dfd42420241b9d64b30d0d268b1feb03b0a5c96",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "A framework diagram showing four levels of action: preventing HIV in all women, preventing unintended pregnancy and transmission to infants among women with HIV, and providing care and support.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "source": "sections/sec-004-a-comprehensive-approach-to-prevent-hiv-infectio.md",
      "source_hash": "fbeb50f33318c708e593e8ee9207ba799332382f18e8ee5ac3c3a241ece1a3fe",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Gives WHO estimates for Africa showing antenatal care coverage averaging 62% and professionally attended deliveries averaging 36%.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "source": "sections/sec-005-specific-interventions-to-reduce-mother-to-child.md",
      "source_hash": "5253d87a8d3f6280e5e19fb5347ae1835b510b9328122c2e03a9968940325871",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes specific interventions to reduce mother-to-child HIV transmission, including antiretroviral regimens chosen locally for feasibility, efficacy and cost, and safer delivery practices that limit invasive procedures. It gives infant-feeding advice: avoiding breastfeeding where replacement feeding is acceptable, feasible, affordable, sustainable and safe, and otherwise exclusive breastfeeding in the first months.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "source": "sections/sec-006-more-than-the-cost-of-drugs-alone.md",
      "source_hash": "9368d4c2f62e59e7e285229174439b05171041ceaebfacb998b1bc5b9636a7d9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Argues that, although antiretroviral drug prices have fallen and donations have expanded access, weak health systems remain the main obstacle. Limited and late use of antenatal care and lack of HIV testing services still hinder delivery of prevention interventions.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-007",
      "source": "sections/sec-007-what-who-is-doing.md",
      "source_hash": "f397b190f0242ae7112fba70805ecafb5528119c71d930960a4d41f2cf11aeee",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States WHO's commitment to work with ministries, agencies, NGOs and people living with HIV to prevent HIV in infants, especially in the hardest-hit countries.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-008",
      "source": "sections/sec-008-highlighting-the-importance-of-prevention.md",
      "source_hash": "263453352631663ebf3fc35d5407a5f3b87190f85d18712a873c129f861ba183",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "States that WHO will keep its focus on preventing HIV among young women as the best way to protect infants.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "source": "sections/sec-009-including-hiv-in-family-planning-programmes.md",
      "source_hash": "e15fe087d8d9d831be092d2e01a07df070d701062e992f5d5c51751563709d90",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes WHO's support for family planning programmes, including promoting dual protection against infection and pregnancy and greater use of male and female condoms.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-010",
      "source": "sections/sec-010-strengthening-the-infrastructure-for-preventing.md",
      "source_hash": "268834203b1cda44d2bd5b7788ab3b4fd6db0324575ec390c4eaaa020400fa27",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Outlines WHO's work to strengthen infrastructure for preventing HIV in infants, including expanding antenatal care through the Making Pregnancy Safer initiative and increasing access to voluntary counselling and testing. It stresses integrating prevention of infant HIV into national health systems.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-67344/blocks/prose-sec-011",
      "source": "sections/sec-011-increasing-access-to-hiv-care.md",
      "source_hash": "503b82e1963f2503875db2ff8e26cebaadfce82a431b14cc4707e4149089e258",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that WHO is expanding access to HIV care in resource-limited settings and developing guidance on care, treatment and support for women identified through prevention programmes and their families.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
